From 36aecbb0aab4c07ca4424d89e3cf38e32fb98983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 09:06:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper_FirstBoot: fire saveNvram;restart_chpass apply
 (factory-reset login lockout fix)

FIELD BUG: after a factory reset + forced admin credential change, users were
locked out at login with their brand-new password (V2 web login rejected -> the
5-fail / 300s lockout, and in SG-mode the permanent "reset to factory" lock).

ROOT CAUSE: Reaper_FirstBoot.asp fired ONLY httpApi.chpass, dropping the
`saveNvram;restart_chpass` apply that stock Main_Password.asp (submitForm) fires
alongside it. Confirmed stock uses the identical action_script (Main_Password.asp
form: action_mode=apply, action_script="saveNvram;restart_chpass"). Two gaps:
  (1) no guaranteed nvram_commit -> the new http_passwd lived in nvram RAM only
      and reverted to the default on the next httpd restart / reboot;
  (2) restart_chpass (-> setup_passwd -> create_passwd, services.c:873/896) never
      ran, so /etc/passwd + /etc/shadow kept the OLD password -> SSH/Samba/FTP and
      the V1 login path were also wrong.
The write itself is otherwise stock-equivalent: chpass -> do_chpass (closed lib)
pw_enc-encrypts http_passwd; V2 login pw_dec's it back and compares. So the store
was fine; the missing commit/shadow-sync was the fault.

FIX: after the (synchronous) httpApi.chpass, submit the existing hidden titleForm
to /start_apply.htm with action_script="saveNvram;restart_chpass" (target=fb_hidden
iframe, so the page never navigates). Runs AFTER chpass so restart_chpass rebuilds
/etc/shadow from the just-committed nvram value. titleForm carries NO http_passwd_x
field, so there is zero risk of a plaintext field overwriting the encrypted value
(safer than stock). Redirect delay 2600->3200ms so the apply/commit lands first.

Router login (web V2 + SSH/Samba via shadow) is now set AND persisted; Wi-Fi is
unaffected (SSID/PSK are set in the separate first-run Wi-Fi step). Shared page ->
propagates to all model branches. METAL confirm: reset -> set password -> reboot
-> log in (should now succeed; nvram http_passwd survives the reboot).
---
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp | 25 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
index 0bb838512d..93b689bcb1 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
@@ -150,7 +150,8 @@ input:focus{border-color:var(--crimson)}
     if(msg){ showErr(msg); return; }
 
     $("fb_go").disabled=true; $("fb_spin").style.display="block";
-    /* same call Main_Password.asp uses -- no bespoke apply path */
+    /* httpApi.chpass is synchronous (async:false) -> http_passwd/http_username are
+       set in nvram (pw_enc-encrypted by do_chpass) before we continue. */
     try{
       httpApi.chpass({
         "restart_httpd":"0",
@@ -163,10 +164,28 @@ input:focus{border-color:var(--crimson)}
       $("fb_go").disabled=false; $("fb_spin").style.display="none";
       return;
     }
+    /* v1.6.6c LOGIN-LOCKOUT FIX: mirror Main_Password.asp, which fires chpass AND a
+       saveNvram;restart_chpass apply. Dropping that apply left two gaps that locked
+       users out with their brand-new password after a factory reset:
+         (1) no guaranteed nvram_commit -> the new http_passwd lived in RAM only and
+             reverted to default on the next httpd restart/reboot;
+         (2) /etc/passwd + /etc/shadow were never rewritten -> SSH/Samba/FTP and the
+             V1 login path kept the OLD password.
+       Reuse the hidden titleForm (posts to /start_apply.htm via the fb_hidden iframe,
+       so it never navigates the page); run it AFTER chpass so restart_chpass rebuilds
+       /etc/shadow from the just-committed nvram value. */
+    try{
+      var tf=$("titleForm");
+      tf.action_script.value="saveNvram;restart_chpass";
+      tf.flag.value="";
+      tf.next_page.value="";
+      tf.submit();
+    }catch(e){}
     /* Changing the admin password may drop this session. Head to "/"; state.js then
        forces the Wi-Fi step (Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp) until a PSK is set, or
-       to the login page to re-authenticate with the new password. */
-    setTimeout(function(){ top.location.href = "/"; }, 2600);
+       to the login page to re-authenticate with the new password. Wait a beat longer
+       than stock (3000ms) so the apply/commit lands before we leave. */
+    setTimeout(function(){ top.location.href = "/"; }, 3200);
   }
 
   document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function(){
-- 
